messages:
maria: Heads-up — I pushed a draft Terraform change for mixed spot/on-demand GPU ASGs to reduce cost while keeping capacity guarantees. Putting it here so folks can comment before I open the PR.

maria: Key points: use an ASG with mixed_instances_policy (launch_template + overrides), capacity-optimized allocation, weighted_capacity so cheaper instance types can count differently, set a small on-demand baseline for safety, add tags for cost center + spot true, and wire the node termination handler via user-data. Example snippet: 
```hcl
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "gpu_pool" {
  name = "gpu-mixed-pool"
  mixed_instances_policy {
    launch_template {
      launch_template_specification {
        launch_template_id = aws_launch_template.gpu.id
        version = "$Latest"
      }
    }
    instances_distribution {
      on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 20
      spot_allocation_strategy = "capacity-optimized"
    }
    override { instance_type = "p4de.24xlarge" weighted_capacity = 8 }
    override { instance_type = "p4d.24xlarge" weighted_capacity = 8 }
    override { instance_type = "g5.48xlarge" weighted_capacity = 4 }
    override { instance_type = "g5.12xlarge" weighted_capacity = 1 }
  }
  mixed_instances_policy_tag {
    key = "bill_to"
    value = "team-llm"
    propagate_at_launch = true
  }
  min_size = 0
  max_size = 40
  desired_capacity = 8
}
```

sam: Nice. A couple of quick questions — how are we setting the base capacity vs desired? if base is 0 then on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity only affects above base, right? Also can we set a fallback to force on-demand if spot failures spike?

maria: Good call. Plan is base_capacity = 2 (in the ASG default config), desired 8 for production pools, and on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 20 so 2 base on-demand + 20% of the remaining. For emergency fallback we rely on autoscaling to scale on-demand when spot capacity is low because of the on_demand_percentage. If we see frequent shortages we can switch allocation_strategy to "lowest-price" temporarily, but capacity-optimized generally reduces interruptions.

leo: Interruption handling — we need to ensure pods drain cleanly. Are we using AWS Node Termination Handler + kube-drain in user-data? Also tag instances with "lifecycle:spot" so our controllers can prefer to evict safely.

maria: Yes. Plan is to bake AMI with node-termination-handler installed and enable the systemd service. Also add a small SSM run-command and user-data hook to call the cluster drain script before shutdown. Example user-data piece: 
```bash
#!/bin/bash
# invoked on instance lifecycle action or spot interruption
/opt/node-termination-handler/drain-node.sh --kubeconfig /etc/kubernetes/kubeconfig || true
# signal ASG lifecycle complete via aws cli (in lifecycle hook flow)
```
Will configure the ASG lifecycle hook in Terraform with a target SQS + lambda to finalize.

jen: FYI — for g5.12x and smaller we saw ENI/IP shortage in dense pod configs which caused networking flakes. If some workloads need lots of pods per GPU consider limiting max-pods per node or preferring the larger instances. Also keep an eye on EBS throughput — some of our eval workloads spike IO.

maria: Noted. We'll set kubelet --max-pods on the launch template and add a Terraform var to prefer larger instance types for heavy-pod profiles. We'll also add an instance metadata tag "gpu_profile": "high_io" to allow scheduler constraints.

sam: How are we going to test before full rollout? Canary in a single AZ? I want to avoid cross-AZ flapping causing regional capacity problems.

maria: Canary plan: create a canary ASG in us-west-2a with desired=2 (mix of spot + on-demand) and run a few long-running eval jobs, then force spot interruptions to validate drain and SSM flows. If green, bump to 25% of capacity, then full. I'll also run Terraform plan and attach the plan to the PR.

deploy-bot: terraform plan:  +1 resource,  +2 modules changed
Plan: 1 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy.
+ aws_launch_template.gpu (new)
+ aws_autoscaling_group.gpu_pool (new)

maria: I added tags: {"team":"llm","bill_to":"team-llm","spot":"true"} on spot overrides so billing shows up. Also adding cloudwatch metrics for spot interruption count per-ASG.

ops-bot: Schedule rollout window after midnight PST Thur-Fri, 2hr maintenance, small canary first. Action items: maria open PR, jen double-check AMI and IO profile, leo validate node-termination-handler config, sam run canary tests. If all good :shipit:

maria: I'll open the PR in ~30m. Thanks for the reviews — will ping here when PR is live. :eyes:
